\subsection*{Abstract}
QIK-VRT combines semantic problem solving with a persistent, source-bound working memory, authorized action paths and verifiable evidence of effects. Its design objective is to improve capabilities and strategies while preserving rules for evidence, provenance, authorization and completion. \src{R1}

A conditional wrapper construction explains how different systems can share interface and evidence semantics. It guarantees neither attainment of every desired state nor universal performance gains. Self-continuity is treated as a verifiable functional profile; subjective experience remains a separate open subject.

Delivery planning addresses distinct products: a personal browser and terminal, interruption-resilient task continuation, Mesh recovery, runtime provisioning, controlled scaling and scientific publication. The decisive issue is the missing transition to use, rather than the number of green jobs or the size of the vision.

