\subsection*{How far does a statement reach?}
\textbf{R / Repository source.} A freshly read file or PR description documents its stated content. A description of implemented functions is not independent evidence of every asserted runtime effect.

\textbf{E / Empirical subject.} A measurement dataset supports only its particular trial: system, load, procedure, sample and time. A successfully completed diagnostic run may specifically document a HOLD.

\textbf{N / Normative task.} Ingolf Lohmann defines the purpose and permitted boundaries. Authorization grants permission to act; it does not prove a theory, an effect or the identity of an external actor.

\textbf{T / Theoretical derivation.} A traceable mathematical construction is identified as such. Without an exact kernel receipt, it receives no machine status \texttt{FORMAL\_PROVED} in this edition.

\textbf{I / Interpretation.} Terms such as developmental leap or collective functional consciousness identify a reasoned interpretation or definition. Naming them does not settle their historical significance.

\textbf{Z / Future or hypothesis.} Dates are planning windows under explicit assumptions. They are not delivery guarantees derived from millisecond measurements.

